<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — VolcengineTLSProducer (release candidate source).

  Current source inventory:
    - The SDK does not track users (NSPrivacyTracking = false).
    - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is intentionally empty. The SDK does not
      autonomously capture user, device, crash, usage, or diagnostic data; it
      only transmits log contents explicitly supplied by the integrating app.
      The app developer remains responsible for declaring the actual payload
      categories, linkage, purposes, and tracking behavior in the app's privacy
      disclosures. An empty array does not mean that caller-supplied logs stay
      on-device.
    - The persistent Core path uses POSIX stat(2) to inspect the size and other
      metadata of WAL files inside the app container. Apple classifies stat as
      NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp; C617.1 is the approved reason
      for metadata access to files inside the app container.
    - The Core also uses POSIX clock_gettime for condition-variable deadlines
      and elapsed timers. Apple's current required-reason SystemBootTime list
      names systemUptime and mach_absolute_time, not clock_gettime, so this
      manifest does not invent a SystemBootTime declaration for that API.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
